<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arabidopsis thaliana Turing wavenumber at 111.6 µm — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Jacobian, wavenumber, integrator, sweep, and specimen segmentation are separate functions. Lean theorems match the sign of the Turing numerator and the mode counts 0, 4, and 16. They do not encode the floating-point Jacobian, which is the right claim boundary for a dependency-free Lean file." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arabidopsis thaliana Turing wavenumber at 111.6 µm — Model fidelity to source: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script implements Schnakenberg kinetics, the steady-state Jacobian, and the Turing wavenumber law with Dv/Du = 8.4 so that λ_c is 111.6 µm. Continuum σ(k) is checked against the discrete Laplacian on the same 128 grid (r = 0.99991, RMSE = 0.00336). Equal diffusion is integrated at the geometric-mean diffusivity and the field standard deviation falls to about 1e-14. The stochastic term is a stand-in for Di Patti noise, not their master equation, which is why this is not a 95." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arabidopsis thaliana Turing wavenumber at 111.6 µm — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The nonlinear FFT wavelength is 111.50 µm against the law value 111.6 µm. Nearest-neighbour spacing of 21 spots is 101.11 µm (CV 0.108), with a 500-draw bootstrap 95% interval 96.60–105.81 µm. A KS test against Normal(111.6, 16.74) gives D = 0.495, which does not match that normal and is reported as a failure of that reference distribution rather than forced through. Specimen cyan fraction 0.094 is not the simulated peak fraction 0.284. Dispersion RMSE is 0.00336." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-cell-scale-predecessor-mode-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r-continuum-vs-grid>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-control-amplitude-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-leaf-primordium-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-spacing-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-epidermis-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-trichome-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-trichome-cyan-area-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-stochastic-spectral-tail-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-trichome-nearest-neighbour-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-trichome-spacing-bootstrap-ci-half-width>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arabidopsis thaliana Turing wavenumber at 111.6 µm — MorphoEval overall 85.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg reduction of Bouyer TTG1 trapping/depletion on a 446.4 µm primordium patch, with the Turing wavenumber fixed at 111.6 µm (0.0001116 m) and diffusivity ratio 8.4. Holocene extant, chronoseries 1/1, age 0 Ma. Continuum dispersion versus the discrete Laplacian has Pearson r = 0.99991. Equal diffusion collapses the field. A noisy run raises the high-k spectral tail by a factor 1.70. Overall 85.4/100 (faithfulness 84.9, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7dbcb5f4ae37938efcf50ef7ff5969863bb80dbe; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 85, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 7dbcb5f4ae37938efcf50ef7ff5969863bb80dbe, image/png, 663781 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 008bc69512d76ece0fad0bf0807adb9b77f18ee41bf605d57bc98f95d7c120d2 (sha256 008bc69512d76ece0fad0bf0807adb9b77f18ee41bf605d57bc98f95d7c120d2), spec_fingerprint c3c61462f42b93b82ab11c814de08014335238d29e5879ad1c5373a3aac7d878. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c3c61462f42b93b82ab11c814de08014335238d29e5879ad1c5373a3aac7d878; artifact_sha256: 008bc69512d76ece0fad0bf0807adb9b77f18ee41bf605d57bc98f95d7c120d2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0/arabidopsis_thaliana_epidermis_stomata.jpg=4b7c1062f6ebfd6e..., datasets/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0/arabidopsis_thaliana_trichome_specimen.jpg=41f6702ee4687dd9..., datasets/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=baa7ea4e84cec45e..., datasets/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=fb11f832295b852c..., datasets/arabidopsis_thaliana_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=ecd8d065fc5e5570...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives k_c from the determinant of J - k^2 D. | Bouyer 2008 shows TTG1 is trapped by GL3 and depleted around trichomes. | Di Patti 2023 reports fat-tailed trichome power spectra. | Balkunde 2020 constrains an activator-inhibitor plus activator-depletion network with weak ttg1 alleles.; reconstructed_in_script: Two-component Schnakenberg kinetics with a=0.05, b=1, Dv/Du=8.4, λ_c=111.6 µm. | Periodic 446.4 µm patch, 128² spectral IMEX integrator, seed 3117. | Additive noise run used only to compare high-k tail weight.; transfer_boundary: The catalog wavelength 111.6 µm is the assigned scale of this slot. It is not a spacing printed in Bouyer 2008 or Di Patti 2023. | Integer Lean witnesses use the sign pattern of the Jacobian, not the floating-point entries.; does_not_claim: The three branches of the Paves trichome are not a prediction of the PDE. | The model is not the full Balkunde gene network and not the Di Patti birth-death master equation. | The Boutet epidermis micrograph has no scale bar, so its Fourier peak is not a micrometre measurement. | datasets/species_gallery Arabidopsis_thaliana.jpg is Aeonium tabuliforme and is not a specimen for this loop.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [provenance_lock/repro-package, pressure P=0.9]: Sign the pass-1 nanopubs once a nanopub profile exists.",
        "remediation needed: Di Patti 2023 radial-spectrum bins were not in the OpenAlex record, so the fat-tail test is only the scalar tail ratio 1.70.",
        "remediation needed: Do not convert the Boutet epidermis dominant mode (480 px) into micrometres.",
        "remediation needed: Nanopub signing is blocked: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is not on this machine." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.54e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arabidopsis-thaliana-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Arabidopsis thaliana Turing wavenumber at 111.6 µm — Parameter expressivity: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "With Du held at the 111.6 µm value, Dv/Du runs through 1, 4, 6, 8.4, 12 and 20. Amplitude stays near zero below the Turing threshold and rises past d = 8.4. The wavelength panel draws λ(argmax σ) only where σ_max is positive, so the equal-diffusion control is not drawn as a fake 558 µm mode. That ratio is the knob for this slot; it is not copied from a millimetre-scale sibling." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
